    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/modality> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Deontic>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/operator> "Believes";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Belief of authorized conduct";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in the ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary offence if, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she believed the related conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged in, by a participant in an operation authorised under a corresponding State controlled operations law.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in the ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary offence if, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she believed the related conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged in, by a participant in an operation authorised under a corresponding State controlled operations law.";
